      "status": "completed",
      "finalText": "Out of 16 leads created last week (Oct 26 – Nov 1), 5 haven't replied and don't have a meeting booked. Each now has an owner and a follow-up task due tomorrow (2026-11-05, medium priority).\n\n| Lead | Owner | Follow-up task |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ravi Haddad (ld_009) | Priya Shah (usr_003), newly assigned | tsk_031 |\n| James Williams (ld_003) | Dana Cruz (usr_005), newly assigned | tsk_032 |\n| Jack Rossi (ld_015) | Jordan Lee (usr_002), already his lead, kept | tsk_033 |\n| Aisha Kim (ld_005) | Jordan Lee (usr_002), newly assigned | tsk_034 |\n| Zoe Patel (ld_011) | Priya Shah (usr_003), newly assigned | tsk_035 |\n\nThe new assignments were spread across the three available sales reps (Jordan Lee, Priya Shah, Dana Cruz). Marcus Reed (usr_004) was left out because he's marked out of office.\n\n**Left out (11 leads):**\n- **Replied:** Mike Smith (ld_002), Carlos Martin (ld_006), Nina Chen (ld_012), Amara Kim (ld_014), Olivia Walker (ld_008)\n- **Meeting already booked:** Sarah Chen (ld_001), Noah Singh (ld_007), Isabel Smith (ld_013)\n- **Both replied and has a meeting:** Priya Okafor (ld_004), Lucas Johnson (ld_010), Sofia Nguyen (ld_016)\n\n**Worth checking:** Mike Smith, Carlos Martin, Nina Chen, Amara Kim and Olivia Walker are still waiting on an answer from us. They wrote last and their conversations are unread. Mike Smith (ld_002) also has no owner.\n\nIf you want this to happen every week, I can set up a workflow that assigns new leads and creates a follow-up task when they don't reply.",
